{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"prime ideal prime ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","fileName":"Prime Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Prime Ideal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra]] · [[Quotient Rings and Ideals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Integral Domain","Spectrum of a Ring","Maximal Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"prime ideal prime ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","fileName":"Prime Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Prime Ideal","heading":"Prime Ideal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A proper [[Ideal]] p is prime when ab ∈ p implies a ∈ p or b ∈ p. Equivalently, the [[Quotient Ring]] R/p is an [[Integral Domain]].\n\nPrime ideals form the points of the [[Spectrum of a Ring]]. They also control radicals, localization, dimension, and primary decomposition. Every [[Maximal Ideal]] is prime because a field is an integral domain.\n\nThe source proves the quotient characterization alongside maximal ideals: a proper ideal is prime exactly when its quotient has no zero divisors. This supplies a structural test that avoids checking the product condition directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Integral Domain","Spectrum of a Ring","Maximal Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"prime ideal prime ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Prime Ideal.md","fileName":"Prime Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Prime Ideal","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Integral Domain","Spectrum of a Ring","Maximal Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}